                  "blocks": {
                    "text_pxiq3K": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>The <strong>Forge Pro</strong> is a <strong>plug-and-play computing device</strong> designed for independent, standalone operation. It allows users to interact with and observe how dedicated computing systems function without relying on external controllers, computers, or third-party services.</p><p></p><p>The device runs continuous, automated processing routines, providing a hands-on way to explore how specialized hardware operates in real-world conditions. All functionality is hardware-based and designed for learning, experimentation, and system observation.</p><p></p><p></p><p></p><h3><strong>Understanding the Operation</strong></h3><p></p><p><br/></p><p>Forge Pro is intended as an <strong>educational and experimental device</strong>. Its operation does not involve guaranteed outcomes, performance benchmarks, or results of any kind. Users should view the device as a way to better understand standalone computing behavior rather than as a performance-driven or outcome-based system.</p><p></p><p><br/><strong>Independent Operation:</strong> The device functions entirely on its own without shared resources or pooled systems.<br/><br/><strong>User Control:</strong> Configuration and operation remain fully under the user’s control at all times.<br/></p><p></p>",
                        "width": "100%",
